			"date": "2025-03-26T01:04:25.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> by headcount the overwhelming number of open source developers are paid a living wage and have been for years. For example there are thousands of full time Linux developers and Android OSP is almost entirely developed by paid professionals. </p><p>There are very few successful OSS projects anymore that are entirely or even mostly developed by volunteers, although some of them are critical infrastructure.</p>",
